  "prompt": "Precise local anatomy repair of IMAGE1 (run W06 v8). Image2 W05v6 shows the correct single continuous NEAR LEFT sleeve crossing the chest; Image3 is approved style. Keep Image1's entire pose, head, face, ribbon, torso placement, both existing hand positions, scroll/brush/spirits, legs/boots and transparent canvas unchanged.\n\nThe error to remove is the EXTRA OPEN EMPTY SLEEVE hanging on the FRONT-RIGHT of the chest, below the near shoulder and right of the round taiji charm. There must NOT be an intermediate dangling cuff there. Redraw that local area into ONE SINGLE CONTINUOUS NEAR LEFT ARM: begin at the existing near shoulder just screen-right below the neck, upper arm slopes diagonally down-left ACROSS the chest, elbow rests in front of chest, forearm connects leftward to the EXISTING scroll grip. This continuous big black-gold sleeve covers part of the collar/charm and has ONLY ONE white/teal open cuff, the existing cuff immediately behind the scroll hand. Close/remove the extra middle open cuff and its dangling teal tassel/flap. Do not invent a third sleeve or third arm. Reference Image2 for the smooth continuous cross-chest sleeve shape; do not transfer its leg pose or scale.\n\nKeep the other FAR RIGHT brush arm and its existing rear hand/sleeve in place: it emerges from behind the torso, on the far side. Exactly2 hands, exactly2 sleeves, one brush/right hand with1 butt tassel, blank scroll/left hand,2cyan spirits. Keep front-facing WEST torso camera, do not turn to back view. Keep original boots, natural knees, support and swing-leg phase pixel placement. No enlargement, recentering, translations, cropping, duplicate limbs or text. Same high-resolution square transparent PNG >=1024px with all elements inside border.",
